# Kernel config fragment: gma-native-net = gma-native-pure + this.
# Applied by linux-port/display/build-net.sh with scripts/config, then olddefconfig.
# Checked 2026-10-09 in the cloud tree (pinned da5f1a22): olddefconfig changes
# exactly LOCALVERSION + these two lines, and vmlinux compiles and links
# (ncm_bind, ncm_alloc_inst present). verify-avprpc.py --variant net enforces it.
CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_NCM=y
# selected automatically by the line above:
CONFIG_USB_F_NCM=y
#
# Already in every gma-native kernel since usbfix (no change needed):
#   CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS=y  CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_ACM=y   (the rescue serial port)
#   CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_RNDIS=y  CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_ECM=y  CONFIG_USB_U_ETHER=y
#   CONFIG_NET=y CONFIG_INET=y CONFIG_IPV6=y CONFIG_PACKET=y CONFIG_UNIX=y
# So RNDIS mode works on the kernel that is on the card now, without a new build.
